    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T12:48:35Z",
    "body": "The mill Z-lift contract does not apply to fanuc-lathe.cps, tormach-lathe.cps, or wire-iso.cps.\nLathe Z runs along the spindle. Fanuc's home path clears X before Z. Tormach's G30 departure orders moves from the stock envelope.\nThe wire post mounts no milling tool. It cuts the wire at section end and refuses a generic home request because it has no home position.\nThese posts keep their current stops, without a new setup-change notification in this fix. The app can send them SetupChange; they need their own verified departure contract before adding a setup-change retract.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
